      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Golem, the endless thread",
      "items": [
        "Each person has one thread that never ends",
        "It answers simple things and hands the rest to a channel thread",
        "A memory tree of 512-byte summaries; zoom opens older messages"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Channels and threads",
      "items": [
        "A thread is one Pi Durable conversation",
        "Answers come back to Golem at most two hops away",
        "Code mode scripts call machines, services, the browser and artifacts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "What carries over",
      "items": [
        "The channel brief is rewritten after 10 quiet minutes",
        "The learning loop keeps facts about people and how-tos",
        "Workspace facts are what the family writes itself"
